--- STEP 1: SURVEY — ADR-009 + notification taxonomy + deep links ----
ADR-009 (live data + push):
  * Foreground live data = SSE (P6-0001). Background = PUSH, never a held stream
    (Doze/iOS suspension kill long streams). iOS → APNs.
  * Apps register device tokens via an additive `/api/v1/devices` endpoint, routed
    through the existing notification-worker. Push provider/credential + Helm wiring
    is per-platform store work (P5 hardening) — OUT of scope here (backend).
  * Historical/series = REST, never SSE replay.

Shared core push surface (apps/shared/core/.../presentation/push):
  PushStore / PushRepository / PushModels = the WEB-PUSH (VAPID) domain
  (`GET|POST|DELETE /push/subscribe`, browser `{endpoint, keys{p256dh,auth}}`).
  OpenAPI (api/openapi/teslasync.openapi.json): NO `/devices` path and NO `/push`
  path emitted yet → the ADR-009 native `/devices` APNs-token endpoint is genuine
  additive backend work not yet present. `ApiHttpClient.request<T>` is `inline
  reified` (NOT exported to Swift/ObjC). => the native `/devices` registration is
  coded against a Shared-free `DeviceRegistering` seam with a real URLSession-backed
  `HTTPDeviceRegistrar` using the P5 auth seams (the facade's auth); the shared-core
  wiring is macOS-pinned exactly like AppContainer.bootstrap / SharedLiveStreamProvider.

Notification categories (web features/notifications + alert severity info|warn|critical),
mapped to native push categories + deep-link AppRoute (web App.tsx route groups):
  alert       -> .notifications   (/alerts alias -> notifications)
  charging    -> .charging        (/charging)
  command     -> .vehicles        (command result; /vehicles, optional vehicle id)
  automation  -> .automations     (/automations)
  security    -> .vehicleSystems  (security event; /vehicle-systems)
  trip/drive  -> .trips           (/trips)
  generic     -> .dashboard
Deep link resolution reuses AppRouteParser.parse(url:)/parse(path:) when the APNs
payload carries an explicit `deeplink`/`route`; else falls back to category->route.

Seam convention reused from the Live module (P6-0001):
  * Shared-free protocol/closure seam + @Observable coordinator/store.
  * Production adapter pinned on the macOS build; tests use fakes (no APNs/ActivityKit
    runtime needed). Redacted PushLog delegates to AuthLog.redact (ADR-016: no
    token/PII logging — device tokens are masked, never logged raw).

DESIGN DECISIONS:
  * APNs token lifecycle: request authorization (localized rationale) -> on grant
    registerForRemoteNotifications -> didRegister hands the token to PushCoordinator
    -> register `/devices` via the seam; permission revocation/foregrounding re-syncs;
    sign-out / disable unregisters. Token is masked in all logs.
  * Foreground UX: UNUserNotificationCenter willPresent -> options gated by quiet
    hours + per-category enablement; in-app banner via the shared feedback components.
  * Live Activities: ActivityKit (charging / drive / command) behind
    `#if canImport(ActivityKit)` + `@available(iOS 16.1, *)` + a LiveActivityPresenting
    seam; macOS / unsupported OS resolve to a NoopLiveActivityPresenter (honest no-op,
    no placeholder UI). Lock-screen/Dynamic-Island UI lives in an iOS widget extension
    (NotificationsExtension/, outside Sources/ so the macOS host typecheck skips it).
  * Settings: authorization status, per-category toggles, quiet-hours window, critical
    alert eligibility, localized privacy copy; persisted via a UserDefaults seam.

